kunzite: Adreno 710, glue plan K0 (main repo ios/gpu-glue-plan.md 3.7): topaz's A610 driver out of
the build, the hardware interface from kunzite_adreno.c, and step 20's gen7_start with hbb 14.
iokit/conf/files.arm64 no longer lists TopazAdreno.cpp and TopazAdrenoFw.cpp (the sources stay,
unbuilt; their A610 zap and A630 SQE arrays, about 41 KB, go with them). kunzite_adreno.c defines,
by their C names, the 21 functions RedwoodGPU.cpp, SweetSurface.cpp and SweetFramebuffer.cpp took
from TopazAdreno.cpp and its variable gpu_log (RedwoodGPU's per-submission trace switch, never set;
the first CI run of this patch failed to link without it), plus redwood_gpu_on() for K5: the SMMU
translates (identity false), no GPU pool (alloc 0, md NULL), never ready until keep mode (K1), so
RedwoodGPU's user client does not start and RedwoodGPUStart() is not called; redwood_gpu_to_memory
is the real thing (dc civac, dsb); topaz_adreno_init() (AppleCLCD::start) only says that gpu=1 has
no driver now. The probe no longer refuses gpu=1. Step 20 programs hbb 14 instead of gen7_3_0's 15,
as kgsl gen7_init does on LPDDR4X (of_fdt_get_ddrtype() == 7; the live FDT's /memory has
ddr_device_type = <0x07>): RB_NC_MODE_CNTL 0x814 -> 0x812, TPL1_NC_MODE_CNTL 0x4 -> 0x2,
SP_NC_MODE_CNTL 0x24 -> 0x22, GRAS_NC_MODE_CNTL 0x40 -> 0x20, UCHE_MODE_CNTL 0x400000 -> 0x200000
(boot #45's fills were linear, so nothing seen depended on it). Test: boots as before without GPU
boot-args; kgpu=22 passes as on boot #45; nm has no _topaz_fw_sqe_fw and has _redwood_gpu_ready.

